WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.838
Delegate Agent solves a practical command line problem.

00:00:03.291 --> 00:00:05.032
You may want a child coding runtime to

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.391
review a diff, investigate a failure, or implement

00:00:08.424 --> 00:00:11.512
a scoped change, but each runtime expects different

00:00:11.557 --> 00:00:15.199
flags, prompt delivery, safety controls, and output

00:00:15.244 --> 00:00:18.886
formats. This repository wraps those differences in

00:00:18.976 --> 00:00:20.559
one Python CLI.

00:00:21.079 --> 00:00:23.839
The same command surface can launch Cursor Agent,

00:00:24.121 --> 00:00:27.820
Factory Droid, OpenAI Codex, Claude Code,

00:00:28.147 --> 00:00:30.805
or Kimi Code, while keeping local records that

00:00:30.861 --> 00:00:32.411
parent agents can inspect later.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.419
The top-level path is deliberately small.

00:00:35.747 --> 00:00:37.782
A thin launcher hands off to the main

00:00:37.862 --> 00:00:40.723
CLI module, and that module owns the control

00:00:40.779 --> 00:00:44.511
flow. It parses arguments, resolves the workspace,

00:00:44.964 --> 00:00:48.661
loads configuration, builds a request object, and decides

00:00:48.695 --> 00:00:50.516
whether the run is a dry run, a

00:00:50.584 --> 00:00:53.637
tracked launch, or a persistent worktree launch.

00:00:54.259 --> 00:00:57.256
Configuration is layered so local automation can be

00:00:57.301 --> 00:00:59.744
predictable without hiding operator settings.

00:01:00.139 --> 00:01:01.711
Embedded defaults come first.

00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:06.201
User config, workspace config, and an environment

00:01:06.269 --> 00:01:08.192
override layer on top of those defaults.

00:01:08.643 --> 00:01:12.319
The validator checks provider sections, policy, reasoning

00:01:12.375 --> 00:01:16.152
declarations, tracking, retention, isolation,

00:01:16.186 --> 00:01:19.025
and worktree settings before any child process starts.

00:01:19.647 --> 00:01:21.479
The first safety idea is mode.

00:01:21.875 --> 00:01:24.284
Safe mode is for review and investigation.

00:01:24.679 --> 00:01:26.614
Work mode is edit capable.

00:01:27.065 --> 00:01:29.361
This boundary is separate from reasoning effort.

00:01:29.757 --> 00:01:31.996
A higher reasoning effort can ask a model

00:01:32.041 --> 00:01:34.359
to think more, but it does not change

00:01:34.416 --> 00:01:38.114
sandboxing, network access, approval mode, or edit

00:01:38.148 --> 00:01:41.846
permission. The second safety idea is isolation.

00:01:42.298 --> 00:01:45.261
Safe runs normally execute in a temporary detached

00:01:45.295 --> 00:01:49.490
worktree or a directory copy, so ordinary relative-path

00:01:49.625 --> 00:01:52.091
edits do not touch the source checkout.

00:01:52.804 --> 00:01:54.805
Work runs can stay in the source checkout,

00:01:55.257 --> 00:01:58.039
or they can create a preserved Git worktree

00:01:58.085 --> 00:01:59.599
and branch for later review.

00:02:00.312 --> 00:02:02.494
Each runtime gets a tailored harness.

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:05.084
Cursor and Kimi still pass the prompt through

00:02:05.107 --> 00:02:08.183
the argument vector, so Delegate redacts prompt text

00:02:08.307 --> 00:02:10.025
in public arguments and manifests.

00:02:10.422 --> 00:02:12.458
Droid uses a private prompt file.

00:02:12.853 --> 00:02:15.691
Codex and Claude receive prompts over standard input,

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:17.942
which keeps task text out of the process

00:02:17.976 --> 00:02:21.504
arguments. When tracked execution begins,

00:02:21.719 --> 00:02:24.150
Delegate creates a local run record under dot

00:02:24.196 --> 00:02:27.599
delegate. The runner writes a manifest, mutable state,

00:02:27.927 --> 00:02:31.489
a bounded snapshot, standard output and standard error

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:35.120
logs, stream events, and sometimes a completion report.

00:02:35.515 --> 00:02:38.682
These files are local runtime state, not source

00:02:38.727 --> 00:02:39.654
files to commit.

00:02:39.982 --> 00:02:42.266
Those records power the inspection commands.

00:02:42.786 --> 00:02:44.879
Runs lists recent or active runs.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:48.916
Snapshot shows current status, isolation details,

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:52.048
recent events, and bounded assistant text.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:55.248
Run output selects the best parent facing result,

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:58.290
then falls back to recovered final text or

00:02:58.358 --> 00:02:59.908
bounded log diagnostics.

00:03:00.428 --> 00:03:02.803
Persistent worktrees add a full lifecycle.

00:03:03.255 --> 00:03:05.438
Delegate checks that Git has a valid head,

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:08.570
the source checkout is clean, pass through mode

00:03:08.593 --> 00:03:10.990
is off, and the child binary exists.

00:03:11.443 --> 00:03:13.964
It then creates a branch, launches the child

00:03:14.009 --> 00:03:17.334
in the worktree, records review commands, and later

00:03:17.413 --> 00:03:20.828
refuses unsafe cleanup unless the caller opts in.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:23.633
The codebase is intentionally lean.

00:03:24.153 --> 00:03:27.128
Runtime Python dependencies are zero.

00:03:27.455 --> 00:03:30.757
The current tracked snapshot is dominated by Python,

00:03:30.916 --> 00:03:32.849
with about twenty nine thousand lines.

00:03:33.245 --> 00:03:35.608
Tests are larger than source, which matches the

00:03:35.677 --> 00:03:39.352
project's focus on command contracts and safety boundaries.

00:03:40.065 --> 00:03:42.360
The main maintenance hotspot is the main CLI

00:03:42.416 --> 00:03:46.024
module. It is the coordination center for parsing,

00:03:46.352 --> 00:03:50.174
request building, prompt framing, temporary isolation,

00:03:50.208 --> 00:03:51.554
and runtime dispatch.

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:55.794
Worktree management is the next hotspot, because cleanup,

00:03:55.952 --> 00:03:59.322
dirty state, merge checks, and registry drift all

00:03:59.379 --> 00:04:02.477
meet there. If you are contributing, choose the

00:04:02.546 --> 00:04:05.836
subsystem first. Runtime flag changes start in the

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:09.071
CLI module. Registry and output changes start in

00:04:09.105 --> 00:04:11.072
the runner and run-output modules.

00:04:11.694 --> 00:04:14.804
Persistent worktree changes start in the isolation and

00:04:14.872 --> 00:04:18.219
worktree-management modules. You can remember Delegate as three

00:04:18.265 --> 00:04:21.204
layers. First, the CLI builds a safe and

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:24.506
explicit request. Next, the runner records what the

00:04:24.552 --> 00:04:25.931
child runtime does.

00:04:26.451 --> 00:04:29.380
Finally, inspection and worktree commands make the result

00:04:29.471 --> 00:04:32.219
usable without guessing where the logs went.
